menu "SPI NAND Flash configuration"

    config NAND_FLASH_VERIFY_WRITE
        bool "Verify SPI NAND flash writes"
        default n
        help
            If this option is enabled, any time SPI NAND flash is written then the data will be read
            back and verified. This can catch hardware problems with SPI NAND flash, or flash which
            was not erased before verification.

    config NAND_FLASH_ENABLE_BDL
        bool "Enable Block Device Layer (BDL) support"
        depends on IDF_INIT_VERSION >= "6.0"
        default n
        help
            Enable Block Device Layer (BDL) support for SPI NAND Flash. This provides:
            - Standard esp_blockdev_t interface for layered architecture
            - Flash Block Device Layer (raw NAND flash access)
            - Wear-Leveling Block Device Layer (logical sector access with wear leveling)
            - Advanced layered API (spi_nand_flash_init_with_layers)
            When disabled, only the legacy API is available.
            When enabled, the legacy spi_nand_flash_init_device() is not available (returns
            ESP_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED). Use spi_nand_flash_init_with_layers().

            Note: This option requires ESP-IDF >= 6.0 (esp_blockdev component).
            Enabling this on ESP-IDF < 6.0 will result in a build error.

    config NAND_FLASH_PAGE_REGISTER_CACHE
        bool "Enable NAND page-register cache"
        default y
        help
            When enabled, the SPI NAND driver tracks whether the chip's
            internal page register already holds the requested page and
            skips the READ PAGE ADDRESS command (25-100 us) on repeated
            reads of the same page. The cache is invalidated on any
            program, erase, or mark-bad operation, since those overwrite
            the chip's internal register.
            Set to false to disable (no caching, original behaviour).

    config NAND_FLASH_DHARA_META_CACHE
        bool "Cache Dhara metadata reads"
        default n
        help
            Cache exact 132-byte Dhara metadata reads per device, keyed by
            page/offset/length. The number of cache slots is set by
            NAND_FLASH_DHARA_META_CACHE_SLOTS. This experimental option is
            intended for throughput testing.

    config NAND_FLASH_DHARA_META_CACHE_SLOTS
        int "Number of Dhara metadata cache slots"
        depends on NAND_FLASH_DHARA_META_CACHE
        default 2
        range 2 8
        help
            Number of exact 132-byte Dhara metadata entries cached per
            device. Each slot uses DHARA_META_SIZE bytes (~132 bytes), so
            the default of 2 slots uses approximately 280 bytes of device
            memory. Increase for workloads with a larger sequential
            metadata working set; decrease to save RAM.

    config NAND_FLASH_PERF_STATS
        bool "Enable NAND physical operation counters"
        default n
        help
            Count physical page reads, programs, copies, block erases and
            Dhara metadata cache hits/misses per device. Read the counters
            with nand_get_perf_stats() and clear them with
            nand_reset_perf_stats(). Uses 48 bytes per device and adds a
            counter increment to every physical operation. When disabled,
            both functions return ESP_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED.

    config NAND_ENABLE_STATS
        bool "Host test statistics enabled"
        depends on IDF_TARGET_LINUX
        default n
        help
            This option enables gathering host test statistics and SPI NAND flash wear levelling simulation.

endmenu
